{"title":"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following expressions is never a prime number when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is a prime number?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/0/df0b1a26bcdfe4e491db19692e6a6c7d175d73eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } p^2+16 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } p^2+24 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } p^2+26 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } p^2+46 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } p^2+96$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"592\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each expression is in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/f/48ffc74a8a9574cf814a871541bac16687f4c943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2 + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>All prime numbers are of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/2420f75683b05e9dff4bef4e2c9e9eca5d553981.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6k \\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />, AKA they are congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/4/5a4c8202c0044b64eef312b2d3a5cea112ecba8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pm1 \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />. We can utilize this nicely to check for what we are looking for. If the expression is a prime, then\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/a/27aa8ca446fe425ca91ea8456fd4123fc7cc566d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2 + n \\equiv \\pm1 \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"171\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/5/e251035aaeea19e25d58e9574957e6232bb93793.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow (\\pm1)^2 + n \\equiv \\pm1 \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"223\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b93dfb709c22a2894200787dbc9b8281718d30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow 1 + n \\equiv \\pm1 \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"187\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/2/7725d994e68b58baece0a5cd8735ba47b8dc4524.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow n \\equiv (\\pm1) - 1 \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"201\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae2eb8dc3ca2fe8efcf283632cd8656cd2fc736b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow n \\equiv (1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/d/7ed7145c276ab01a92d2cf34d5d0ee3e0a027f24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$or$\" width=\"17\" height=\"8\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c41271a022c27982d8b548c82f5bc55516c498.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1) - 1 \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/8/f28435c2c46fa35f1d9b5b88c0a0ffaf48e29997.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow n \\equiv 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/d/7ed7145c276ab01a92d2cf34d5d0ee3e0a027f24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$or$\" width=\"17\" height=\"8\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a2f8c2473adedf9df84d2a2875a4f7ae0845d8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2 \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\nNow, just check for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> in each option using this condition to check whether its prime or not.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/1/cd1da65768602e24421435d9143ae1445a3cd4e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(A)\\ n = 16; prime\\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/b/1fb6fda555e010ea26a5f9c8af0a2399ee5ae8a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(B)\\ n = 24; prime\\]\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/1296698385b03ebcf650f42f5d1a24d086d25c7b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(C)\\ n = 26; not\\ prime\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/a/5da94386055490f39ac4580a0abb019167414ac4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(D)\\ n = 46; prime\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/e/b3ec64a9c9ff26312722480f21b04de51ba7cf1d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(E)\\ n = 96; prime\\]\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a40169d4399aa52fecec9cc1913a8f26f9e83f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } p^2 + 26}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"105\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>~ <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/b/e6bda7205116585adf73f51ed10342a2ba79b506.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$shalomkeshet$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"114\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because squares of a non-multiple of 3 is always <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91c18a864fecc0092e5be9451ffbc9e9e3bd5d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, the only expression always a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1c51ad580e5291c95b179641c9c6a4f140599e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } p^2+26}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"103\" height=\"31\" />. This is excluding when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b4441e03cdf4b443e6d7476d1d681ae5c789f37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\equiv 0 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" />, which only occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54cfc82a82f113a7432ca68f71338c383bbcb44b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/80661505e712c57c5b7e1888fd01a978f4ac4733.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2+26=35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" /> which is still composite.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>\\( p^2 + 16 \\) is prime for \\( p = 5 \\), so we know that \\( A \\) doesn't work.\n</p><p>Because \\( p^2 + 96 = p^2 + (16) \\cdot 6 \\), we see that eventually there exists a number \\( p \\) that makes the sum prime, therefore \\( E \\) also doesn't work.\n</p><p>Option \\( B \\) is \\( p^2 + 24 \\), but because the number itself has no carryover, we can assume \\( p = 5 \\) again to get the number \\( 41 \\), which is prime.\n</p><p>Option \\( D \\) is \\( p^2 + 46 \\), ending in \\( 6 \\), so we try \\( p = 5 \\) again to get \\( 71 \\). This is also prime.\n</p><p>We can either deduce through elimination that \\( p^2 + 26 \\) is always composite for any prime \\( p \\), but we can prove it by showing \\( p = 5 \\) doesn't work, \\( p = 7 \\) doesn't work, and \\( p = 11 \\) doesn't work, and through <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/Induction?srsltid=AfmBOooY-SKw1NAbaPWjFKkyfSoHj6RXiwWuqty6FtGzCI5GAw7eyCTA\">Engineer's Induction</a>, \\( p^2 + 26 \\) always remains composite.\n</p><p>Therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a40169d4399aa52fecec9cc1913a8f26f9e83f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } p^2 + 26}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"105\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 4 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the question asks which of the following will never be a prime number when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is a prime number, a way to find the answer is by trying to find a value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> such that the statement above won't be true.\n</p><p>A) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f77a117baf37b5430a0615eeb44d952af56fac05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2+16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> isn't true when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/9744b986a275413b1d5e52af4ee4642253f606d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/c/81c92d2a60fca3094cfbe16d9544b81afc3ec6c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25+16=41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" />, which is prime\n</p><p>B) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/7/227a0767da3fb8646d34c7697c2516c78f2874a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2+24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> isn't true when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/9/5f95fee4e5abb16c2f5c07c41672e3a97c63d2de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/e/14e7a96ff198585202a41b212e39e0a0a34144ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49+24=73$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" />, which is prime\n</p><p>C) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/2/e62a3433403778835870265df67130ba765806af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2+26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>D) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/7/ac7d2991e191ce23090212cc7892adfd6142f9ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2+46$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" /> isn't true when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/9744b986a275413b1d5e52af4ee4642253f606d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/0/130489696a91a3d87bec97351f7bd92a35545547.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25+46=71$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" />, which is prime\n</p><p>E) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bff85017a0f9237516858672bc8cbc671f454f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2+96$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> isn't true when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65afa5337178022480485e22da271280652def87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/2/972686758dfe5dec5a5dc0e6d52edc3fd6abd634.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$361+96=457$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"119\" height=\"14\" />, which is prime\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/8/0b8c89e855982fd470ad44d61fdbd31f82c4b129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\framebox{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"23\" /> is the correct answer.\n</p><p>-DAWAE\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Minor edit by Lucky1256. P=___ was the wrong number.\n</p><p>More minor edits by beanlol.\n</p><p>More minor edits by mathmonkey12.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!!!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/PyCyMEBQCXM\">https://youtu.be/PyCyMEBQCXM</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/XRCWccGFnds\">https://youtu.be/XRCWccGFnds</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/3bRjcrkd5mQ?t=187\">https://youtu.be/3bRjcrkd5mQ?t=187</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table